Z||000000||BOILERMAKER||10-05-1999||09:09 AM||||I went to the bone yard last night to see if there were any fieros and saw 2.  After looking through these I decided to try to get the center consoles (the one with the glovebox and the brown piece around the shifter).  Yes, these were the brown pieces.  After agreeing on a $30 price tag for both of them together I went out and got them off.  PERFECT!!!!  After cleaning these babies off, I saw that these puppies were absolutely perfect.<P>Boy boneyards are great!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gokart||10-05-1999||07:12 PM||||I agree! I have two in my area and I've probably saved at least $300.00 on items I would have gone to the Fiero Store for over the last 5 years. Between the two there are about 10 Fieros, but no GT's. I've left my number with them in case they ever get one and I'll buy it outright for parts. ||||reg||14
Z||000002||mshill||10-08-1999||02:30 AM||||Boneyards Rock!!!!  Today I got a 120MPH speedometer, a working fuel/temperature guage, and a passsenger side seat cover for $21 tax included.  I was shooting for the EGR tube, but when I got it off, it was, of course, cracked. <P>I could have spent all day there stripping this 86 GT V6, but I only had one hour before the kids got out if school.  I had to be quick.<P>||||reg||14
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||10-08-1999||01:54 PM||||I wish the boneyards here had some V6 Fieros. I have been to atleast 15 boneyards around here and have only seen 1 V6 Fiero(it was rolled, stripped and half of the frame was left) and about 30 84-86 coupes and 1 87 coupe. I have NEVER seen an 86-88 GT!||||reg||8
